Changes
-------

The copy differs from the original packages in the ways below. The history
of the repository holds each change with its diff.

- The import paths `marker.`, `surya.`, and `pdftext.` are rewritten to
  `raw2md_engine.marker.`, `raw2md_engine.surya.`, and
  `raw2md_engine.pdftext.`.
- The parts that raw2md does not call are removed: the LLM pass, the
  extraction converter, the config parser, the input formats other than
  PDF, the output formats other than Markdown, and the command-line and
  browser applications.
- The PDF converter builds its provider and its Markdown renderer
  directly.
- The settings are fixed values. They do not load from environment
  variables or from a `local.env` file.
- The copy downloads nothing: no font when the converter starts and no
  model weights. `marker/models.py` takes the folder of the weights from
  its caller.
- The models build their non-persistent buffers on the CPU, and the
  loaders build them again after the load of the weights, before the move
  to the device (2026-10-19). Changed files, under
  src/raw2md_engine/surya/: `common/load.py`, `common/adetr/decoder.py`,
  `common/surya/decoder/__init__.py`, `common/surya/encoder/__init__.py`,
  `ocr_error/model/encoder.py`, `foundation/loader.py`,
  `table_rec/loader.py`, and `ocr_error/loader.py`.
- The copy follows the API of transformers 5 (2026-10-19): the tied
  weights as a mapping, `post_init` in every model, the default rotary
  frequencies and the head mask in the copy itself, the tokenizer helpers
  from their new module, and no head pruning or ONNX configuration.
  Changed files, under src/raw2md_engine/surya/: `common/pretrained.py`,
  `common/adetr/decoder.py`, `common/donut/encoder.py`,
  `common/surya/__init__.py`, `common/surya/decoder/__init__.py`,
  `common/surya/decoder/config.py`, `ocr_error/model/config.py`,
  `ocr_error/model/encoder.py`, `ocr_error/tokenizer.py`,
  `table_rec/model/encoder.py`, and `table_rec/model/encoderdecoder.py`.
- The copy fixes defects of its text extraction and its Markdown output,
  drops code that raw2md never runs, and follows the formatting and lint
  rules of raw2md (2026-10-24). Changed files, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  - Text: `pdftext/pdf/pages.py` ignores the blank spans of a line when it
    marks a superscript or a subscript. `marker/schema/text/line.py` keeps
    a dash at the end of a line. `marker/schema/blocks/listitem.py` removes
    only the leading bullet of a list item.
  - Links: `pdftext/pdf/links.py` drops a link whose target is inside the
    document. The page references, the reference processor and block, and
    the span anchors go with it, in `pdftext/schema.py`,
    `pdftext/extraction.py`, `marker/builders/document.py`,
    `marker/providers/`, `marker/schema/`, and
    `marker/renderers/markdown.py`.
  - Tables: `pdftext/tables.py` measures the gap between characters along
    the line and keeps the character boxes of a table run.
    `marker/processors/table.py` splits a run of numbers at the cell
    boundaries and removes dot leaders only outside the values.
    `marker/renderers/markdown.py` escapes a vertical bar in a cell and
    writes one separator line for a table of one row.
  - Formats and math: `marker/schema/text/span.py` applies every format of
    a span, with math innermost and bold outermost, and keeps superscript
    markup out of math. `marker/renderers/__init__.py` keeps the minus when
    two inline math spans merge. `marker/renderers/markdown.py` keeps the
    escaped space at the end of math and removes bold from a heading.
  - Layout: `marker/processors/sectionheader.py` sorts the heading heights
    together with their cluster labels, gives one level to neighboring
    clusters of close mean heights, and keeps headers without lines out of
    the clusters. `marker/processors/ignoretext.py`
    counts the repeats of a running header on the even and the odd pages
    apart.
  - Dead code: `marker/converters/pdf.py` drops the line merge, blank page,
    and block relabel processors, and their files go.
  - Imports: `marker/settings.py` imports torch only when the device is
    read. `surya/common/surya/processor/tokenizer.py` imports no torch and
    builds without a special token file.
  - Style: ruff formats every Python file of the copy and applies its safe
    fixes. `surya/detection/heatmap.py` takes its result class from
    `surya/detection/schema.py`, which breaks an import cycle.
- The Markdown renderer returns the HTML that it converts to Markdown
  (2026-11-01). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/renderers/markdown.py`.
- The PDF converter names each of its steps to an optional phase callback
  before the step runs (2026-11-01). Changed file, under
  src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/converters/pdf.py`.
- The repeated text processor hides a copy of a running header only when
  at least two other copies stand at its height, and its text key keeps a
  number that follows a dot (2026-11-08). Changed file, under
  src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/ignoretext.py`.
- The text fixer keeps fullwidth forms and curly quotes, and repairs the
  rest as before. Math keeps the default configuration (2026-11-11).
  Changed files, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/util.py`,
  `marker/providers/pdf.py`, `marker/builders/ocr.py`, and
  `marker/processors/table.py`.
- A block that OCR reads as a whole keeps the frames of its detector lines,
  and one block method returns the line frames of any block (2026-11-11).
  Changed files, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/builders/ocr.py` and
  `marker/schema/blocks/base.py`.
- A paragraph cut by a page keeps a trailing dash, and it joins without a
  space when Han, kana, or fullwidth punctuation meet at the cut
  (2026-11-11). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/renderers/markdown.py`.
- The text processor joins a paragraph cut by a page, a column, or a
  figure. It steps over pictures, captions, and footnotes, reads the text
  at the cut as well as the line frames, and moves the second half behind
  the first, so the figure follows the joined paragraph. A hyphen `-` at
  the cut stays before a capital or a digit, and a soft hyphen `¬` goes.
  A text block that holds only a label and a number is no half, and a text
  block that repeats on three pages or more is stepped over
  (2026-11-12). Changed files, under
  src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/text.py`,
  `marker/processors/debug.py`, and `marker/renderers/markdown.py`.
- The line height of a block divides the block height by the count of
  detector line frames, so a heading that OCR reads as one text line gets
  the height of one line (2026-11-11). Changed file, under
  src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/schema/blocks/base.py`.
- The nesting of a list item needs the start of its first text line and
  the frame of the item both to move right of the parent (2026-11-12).
  Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/list.py`.
- The equation processor keeps the text of a formula block. A reading
  without math gives the text layer of the block, or a paragraph when the
  block has no text layer. A reading with a word outside its formulas is
  a line with inline math. Any other reading puts each formula on its own
  display line and keeps the punctuation and the numbers between the
  formulas in order. A formula enclosed by brackets or parentheses, or one
  wrapped in square brackets, stays inline on the line under the formula
  before it. A bracketed condition outside the formulas, with a relation
  and no word of three letters or more, is not a word (2026-11-14).
  Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/equation.py`.
- A picture keeps the frame of the layout model, and a detector line goes
  to a picture only when at least half of its area lies inside that frame.
  A text line beside a chart goes to another block by overlap or by
  distance, or to a new text block. A new block whose center equals the
  center of an existing block no longer fails the placement
  (2026-11-13). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/schema/groups/page.py`.
- A new processor hides a picture whose frame lies in the top or the
  bottom 15 % of the page and repeats at one place, each edge within
  0.015 of the page side, on three pages or more. The renderer neither
  shows nor saves a hidden picture, and the block stays in the document
  (2026-11-13). Added file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/processors/image_furniture.py`. Changed files:
  `marker/converters/pdf.py` and `marker/renderers/html.py`.
- The Markdown renderer ends each paragraph without continuation without a
  space, so a paragraph that ends in an italic span or an inline formula
  at the foot of a page does not read as a paragraph cut by the page
  (2026-11-13). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/renderers/markdown.py`.
- A table cell joins a line that wraps onto the next line with a space,
  and it keeps each new value on a line of its own. A line wraps when the
  first word of the next line would not fit into the room that the line
  leaves in its column, and the next line starts under it, at most 0.3
  line heights below. The width of a column is its widest line, each line
  counted at most at the width of its cell. A line that opens with a
  bullet is a new value. A hyphen at the end of a wrapped line goes
  before a lowercase letter and stays before a capital or a digit. A cell
  without line frames keeps its lines (2026-11-14).
  Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/table.py`.
- A new processor joins a table that a page break cuts in two. The table
  that closes a page takes the rows of the table that opens the next page,
  when only running headers, footers and hidden blocks stand between them,
  the column counts are equal or differ by one with each column of the
  narrower part over a column of the wider part, and the first rows of the
  second part repeat the first rows of the first part cell for cell or the
  table model reads its first row as data. Past the first row, only a
  header row repeats. The repeated rows go. A table whose first row
  repeats a run of its own cells, records set side by side, stays apart,
  and so does a part where a header row did not repeat or a cell spans
  over the cut. A table cell keeps the header flag of its row from the
  table model (2026-11-14). Added file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/processors/table_merge.py`. Changed files:
  `marker/converters/pdf.py`, `marker/processors/table.py` and
  `marker/schema/blocks/tablecell.py`.
- The text processor reads the first line of a second half as indented
  when it starts right of the leftmost line by more than a tolerance. When
  the text at the cut shows a continuation, the tolerance is 1.5 units or
  0.02 of the block width, whichever is larger, so one step of the line
  frames is no indent wherever the block stands on the page. Without that
  text, an offset of more than 0.01 units is an indent (2026-11-15).
  Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/: `marker/processors/text.py`.
- The text processor joins two text blocks of one page that stand one
  right under the other with no block between them, when the text at the
  cut shows a continuation and the second block does not start indented.
  The gap between the blocks is less than half the median line height of
  the first block and more than minus half of it. The blocks overlap
  along the horizontal axis by at least half the width of the narrower
  block (2026-11-15). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/processors/text.py`.
- The table merge processor also joins a table that a column break cuts
  on one page. The table that ends a column takes the rows of the table
  that opens the next column, when the second part starts no lower than
  the first and right of its right edge, only running headers, footers
  and hidden blocks stand between them, and the conditions of a page
  break hold. Each column of one part also overlaps its column of the
  other part, with the edges measured as a share of the width of their
  own table (2026-11-15). Changed file, under src/raw2md_engine/:
  `marker/processors/table_merge.py`.

Each changed file of `pdftext/` carries a notice at its top.

